2026-03-28 23:50:40 - DEBUG - text=The future of video games looks bright, with developments in artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning, and blockchain technology poised to revolutionize the industry., The introduction of 8-bit and 16-bit graphics allowed for more detailed and colorful game worlds, enhancing the immersive experience for players., The 1970s saw the rise of arcade gaming, with games like Pong, Space Invaders, and Pac-Man becoming cultural phenomena., The success of arcade games paved the way for the development of home gaming consoles, such as the Atari 2600, which brought the arcade experience into people's living rooms., One of the earliest video games, Spacewar!, was developed in 1962 at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) and is considered a milestone in the history of video game development., The 1980s marked a golden age for video games, with the release of iconic games like Super Mario Bros., The Legend of Zelda, and Tetris., target_entity=blockchain technology, related_kg=none, result=content='{\n  "central_entity": {\n    "name": "blockchain technology",\n    "type": "Technology",\n    "description": "Blockchain technology is a decentralized digital ledger system that is poised to revolutionize the video game industry.",\n    "attributes": [\n      {\n        "key": "Impact on Video Games",\n        "value": "Revolutionizing the industry"\n      },\n      {\n        "key": "Associated Technologies",\n        "value": "Artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning"\n      }\n    ],\n    "relationships": [\n      {\n        "relation": "Revolutionizing",\n        "target_name": "video games",\n        "target_type": "Industry",\n        "target_description": "The video game industry involves the development, marketing, and sale of video games across various platforms.",\n        "relation_description": "Blockchain technology is set to revolutionize the video game industry by enabling new features and systems."\n      },\n   