2026-03-29 00:33:33 - DEBUG - text=Pollination is the process by which pollen is transferred from the male reproductive organs of a flower to the female reproductive organs, leading to fertilization and the production of seeds and fruits., As bees collect nectar and pollen from flowers, they inadvertently transfer pollen from one flower to another, facilitating cross-pollination and increasing genetic diversity within plant populations., Without bees, many crops would require expensive and labor-intensive hand pollination, leading to higher production costs and lower yields., In conclusion, bees play a vital role in agriculture as pollinators, contributing to the success of crop production and the health of ecosystems., The decline of bee populations in recent years has raised concerns about the sustainability of agriculture and the health of ecosystems., This decline poses a serious threat to food security, as well as the health of natural ecosystems., In addition to crop pollination, bees also play a vital role in maintaining the health of natural ecosystems., target_entity=Pollen, related_kg=none, result=content='{\n  "central_entity": {\n    "name": "Pollen",\n    "type": "Biological Substance",\n    "description": "Pollen is a fine powder produced by the male reproductive organs of flowering plants, essential for the process of pollination and plant reproduction.",\n    "attributes": [\n      {\n        "key": "Function",\n        "value": "Transfer for fertilization and seed production"\n      },\n      {\n        "key": "Source",\n        "value": "Male reproductive organs of flowers"\n      },\n      {\n        "key": "Role in Ecosystems",\n        "value": "Facilitates plant reproduction and supports biodiversity"\n      }\n    ],\n    "relationships": [\n      {\n        "relation": "Transferred By",\n        "target_name": "Bees",\n        "target_type": "Animal",\n        "target_description": "Bees are insects that collect nectar and pollen from flowers